<title>HONG KONG: Hongkong Telecom shares jump to new high.</title>
<headline>Hongkong Telecom shares jump to new high.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd shares soared to new highs on Friday on renewed speculation that China's Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications (MPT) may take a stake in the company, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;There is a story in the Chinese press about asset swaps between the MPT and Hongkong Telecom,&quot; said Archie Hart in institutional sales at BZW Securities Asia.</p>
<p>Hongkong Telecom leaped to an all-time high of HK$18.35 in early Friday trade, then eased back a bit to trade up HK$1.05 at HK$18.15 in late morning.</p>
</text>
